  "source_name": "https://www.whattoexpect.com/toddler/potty-training/potty-training-rewards",
  "source_type": "website",
  "structure": {
    "block_count": 58,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "20 Rewards That Will Help Your Child Master Potty Training, According to Doctors",
        "text_sha256": "7c8cccd59c3d2095c79b676b2f636bfc2468117d1a49b1ccf53784af8c9a52f6",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Updates to copy, sources, and formatting.",
        "text_sha256": "2bf448333081ffc8549a45a6c4b7fc711ee4b93575f0fffd3c4a6212c13581c2",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "potty training rewards, hand holding a small pink trophy in front of a beige background",
        "text_sha256": "68156538e09bcbfa9c73cdf0fc09a790108976ff8b8c418a53412410633d90ff",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Little incentives can go a long way in helping your child learn to use the potty.",
        "text_sha256": "4e57787da680941c0362cc69c2635088dc3d8b9fa93d4d9642e12b919de265a2",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You're ready to ditch the diapers , but your toddler may be hesitant to leave them behind. That's understandable. After all, your tot has been wearing diapers his entire life — and now, he's supposed to use the potty on command (and recognize when he has to use the potty, and make it to the potty…).",
        "text_sha256": "0163292236a5729881e1f6b71143f299cad53a3ad18738dc28585e003c40b35f",
        "word_count": 56
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "So it only makes sense that some toddlers resist toilet training even when they're physically ready. Luckily, M&Ms aren't your only option for incentivising your tot to use the toilet (although they can certainly work). Here are some more ideas to try.",
        "text_sha256": "002e94904b587134189ee5703cedca4f841fa46c4745d852f87c94504d620f10",
        "word_count": 42
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key-Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "c2a9bcce7698ee0702f3d963a8b82556c80a5c4c5eff821a1c928b50c51d08da",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Rewards can make potty training easier — and that’s okay. Offering small incentives like praise, stickers, or even a tiny treat helps reinforce positive behavior (and it isn't bribery).",
        "text_sha256": "2b1a9b8354c2a63e1130cd0c8ce8bdcb73faa87a5a9af0be272b26dd464fbbb0",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Phase out rewards as your child gains confidence. Start with immediate rewards, then gradually stretch them out until going potty becomes routine — and eventually needs no extra incentive at all.",
        "text_sha256": "62e1adc3f469a209f846f7132ba25fd4f66949035db4a944c4bb134918227015",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Remember, every child is different. Some toddlers are motivated enough by curiosity, comfort, or the excitement of “big kid” underwear, so the potty itself becomes the prize.",
        "text_sha256": "40dddc0a2e800f2c2b0fa8c89b18ae6146d382a0537a410a1cdd2e2f16b7e15c",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Should you offer potty training rewards?",
        "text_sha256": "5c72aa573e45f857096353dc8980798211e7615e06fef3151ab7725941f38b17",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There's nothing wrong with offering your child a small reward once he's ready to start potty training .",
        "text_sha256": "75fb12ad16519e6ffb6945595f0017196b23ee4f0068ba40bde395a4d59616eb",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"You're helping reinforce a positive behavior with something that is more tangible than just thanking the toddler,\" says Alexandra Cvijanovich, M.D. , a spokesperson for the American Academy of Pediatrics (AAP). \"You may also be speeding up the [potty training] process by rewarding it.\"",
        "text_sha256": "b9a77fbc50f9d05500be0cdda163e2eeee430bf6e4ad9ea5422b1b946908b526",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It's true that, for some parents, rewarding a trip to the bathroom sounds a lot like bribery. But there’s a difference. While a \"reward\" is a prize for a job well done, a \"bribe\" implies the parent will do something in return for a child's behavior.",
        "text_sha256": "42982f39b4b7f2b5687e878ce752a43cb5c0a02203bb74bc3e99cff1e00abd8e",
        "word_count": 46
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Plus, \"bribes frequently reinforce negative behavior, such as stopping a tantrum with a piece of candy,\" says Dr. Cvijanovich. \"A reward is simply a reward.\"",
        "text_sha256": "1ebffe95e22f59c80bd7c3b69ae0c5f916397706613d94191564aafdbc45bc1b",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Of course, not all children need a reward when they're ready to potty train , says Francyne Zeltser, PsyD , a child psychologist and clinical director at Manhattan Psychology Group.",
        "text_sha256": "edf2a1609a7a393fec06c08eddc121cd6a3f2d825c1755b834efbdc60b1831a2",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A child who's motivated to use the potty — say, one who's uncomfortable in a dirty diaper, curious about the toilet, or wants to wear underwear like an older sibling — may not need any rewards as the act of successfully using the potty is rewarding in of itself, she says. And that's okay, too.",
        "text_sha256": "f6ba766da4cb5303ce5dffd8156dc6e8c6a3d535e76d54e78c2e3e394baf68cf",
        "word_count": 55
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Potty training reward ideas",
        "text_sha256": "b6c1820587104b2f7623ad75b30b09a633b9a022af7368d891fe7d1d942e98d5",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You don't always have to reward your child with tangible items such as snacks. Zeltser recommends starting with intangible ones, like your attention or approval. If that doesn't work, you could introduce physical incentives, like food or small toys.",
        "text_sha256": "07db03334bb4e33d912c8250143a3fa8eac9616499e3b387d2594bbee01601d0",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Attention rewards",
        "text_sha256": "e47e7df32cdc18eba460a27e74a062cc4c870db28095dcb07ed1893a07cb0d00",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "The good part about offering your child praise is that it's always readily available (and there's no sugar added ). Some things to try include:",
        "text_sha256": "0690ff9a01fe009a5e69684d908d9cc251246d004927758310cec12e69ae71ea",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Praise",
        "text_sha256": "2a9c05a07ef497af6a995aa3113156e6a298b1b3660ec73e9ec42732f1c47b01",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "High fives",
        "text_sha256": "a8c4e3351ade131a27155b4af2f23e4895121806ff2639b94f1f05814e2c2b7e",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "First bumps",
        "text_sha256": "2616af619d08705935612ef20176304f945e31565239f2b22d3c832f82c6832b",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Hugs",
        "text_sha256": "724e850994fee77c9e61b4438a70de5b0d99db3848d539a379cca42ed2448889",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "A silly song or dance",
        "text_sha256": "ba1ac2b93aa2471894e260579af13b28ab5e769c7860fa3b72c712011bc58d81",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Storytime",
        "text_sha256": "c47572b78375273746a8a3c8e029e97fd247a19fa2f5a0f35124875924cc3fe0",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It helps to make your praise specific: Say, \"Great job using the potty!\" or \"Let's read a story now to celebrate you using the potty.\" This helps your toddler associate the positive attention more closely with using the potty.",
        "text_sha256": "54d7787375e1a9290c24855395af68b90f3c7535e63b2b2e8880cb16c1712f8e",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Food rewards",
        "text_sha256": "e247cb4a4f148a44ad42977a8c76d31681eb32bb3384bc135f5b96b1167e9cc7",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If your child needs a little more incentive to use the potty, you can try offering him a small snack or treat. Just be consistent about what rewards he gets and when, Zeltser says.",
        "text_sha256": "08891011ce7ddf033fb42feaee7811ba932df60c0f173eb77dd07df61f0f6401",
        "word_count": 34
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "And if he wants another treat? Hold firm, and remind him that he can have another treat the next time he uses the potty. Here are a few foods to try:",
        "text_sha256": "3639437a89082c01e55ea6cf99b8ecaa31cb1333c6c7451c6a1e17ea646eacc1",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Mini M&Ms",
        "text_sha256": "eb54b3bc852373f4c75ab5a6f8ca70d4f5cd14c6b259d13cf04eb39249e175d7",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Mini marshmallows",
        "text_sha256": "6d818fd9125c0897ea313af0f9e05d65751be39353cabf3234e2319e5aa9ed8c",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Mini chocolate chips",
        "text_sha256": "de32e4545f1b18c0d48bbb6597732b7b8afab6dff59821cc698f77a023196f37",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Whole-wheat pretzels",
        "text_sha256": "cd0025e6bf64661ba1b0fda6459f2cf88de865de1895cb7b43608e9a03910f21",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Fruit slices",
        "text_sha256": "931d04e779b1c00fae5569f7c3b4aaefeeca57a6a794d15682c4f82b38151728",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Crackers",
        "text_sha256": "9df915306473086a9f26f104fae3fe6a59bf5e364b376f42d39c8d57eddd8d0d",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Cereal pieces",
        "text_sha256": "42f82b26ef205af2f38fc763e9d1eda339283c31124730df6546e3ed87a4df9f",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“With my oldest, we do one M&M for peeing in the potty, two if she asks to go,” says What to Expect Community member mybabyishangry.",
        "text_sha256": "1465dc7e7183fadadba5577a3ec92fbdf16e20ffcf7b7591714eae7cde9f359a",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Fun rewards",
        "text_sha256": "23b08c542ce926927000fa51802c24b7e01f4b3ef249ff1511d717ed2d9e375c",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You could also offer small toys or outings as a reward. (Big-ticket items can add up quickly!) Some ideas to try include:",
        "text_sha256": "11bf4e24f8ec1ff9cbba376c90270b9225a8a3fbe7d1c389391f944932d55f04",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Stickers",
        "text_sha256": "dbf9cbbe0d379b63413340aa4637e03670be1b5af170d61dbfc9ebff23561804",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Hand stamps",
        "text_sha256": "1471d9172d3d5d86bd6f0d9cdc7a91d229ec93c813fba730b3834dcc542fd7d3",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Small toys",
        "text_sha256": "bac28734b6684d4ac17221e55fa8246c376348e66a8539e702a969cb8e7f378e",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Art supplies",
        "text_sha256": "fd57f44e3cdf3877bac1acac29286789d944cc4244043556732c6ab6d0663529",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Books",
        "text_sha256": "9da7f76bc81d2f4e5ee6a83817f7a1db2aadbc9ca13726b0c40b6ace756dce0c",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Blocks",
        "text_sha256": "1cd5a6687bb76e3926f8c89a9fb290cd17d893ca944899952322d3fb5c9896d3",
        "word_count": 1
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "A trip to the library, park, or museum",
        "text_sha256": "e48d81876d212df3973986f5017c57e9b17de2cd1f9e1e440d98114ae5f4adec",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000048",
        "block_index": 48,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "“I suggest a sticker chart with a big reward. We did five stickers and he got a prize at the end. He was bored of that quickly, but hasn’t had accidents since day three, so it worked,” says What to Expect Community member julia828.",
        "text_sha256": "0d0245395059cec53d3616b63433b12f578159acfe3376910e8be7aa05b16bdf",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000049",
        "block_index": 49,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Get more tips about potty training and other toddler milestones in the What to Expect app .",
        "text_sha256": "43ca94ef25037f0936cbf3208c955cf233d15c68a0d0a2f24092152023683322",
        "word_count": 17
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000050",
        "block_index": 50,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How to use potty training rewards",
        "text_sha256": "13e02360bccef849530c7238a17a7ed204e1a91c92775c7ee3cf7c52cd078cce",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000051",
        "block_index": 51,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Offer the reward as soon as your little one uses the potty — not, say, at the end of the week. To a toddler, “a week is an eternity,\" says Dr. Cvijanovich.",
        "text_sha256": "bcc3e9272f08b796e9dbd98360b83c2fbb220dc54a26700a4c1bf8a60050d073",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000052",
        "block_index": 52,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you're using a potty training chart — and offering a toy or other fun treat after he goes to the bathroom, say, five or 10 times, for example — give out a sticker or stamp right away, so there's an immediate reward or sign of accomplishment.",
        "text_sha256": "4c14c477ebe2fdb51501167e8b8ebcf627558da5d31cc5021db41956a0e2900f",
        "word_count": 47
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000053",
        "block_index": 53,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If your child is particularly anxious about potty training, you could try giving him an \"over-the-hump\" gift early on, Zeltser says. That way, every time your child feels nervous about using the bathroom, you can encourage him by saying, \"You were able to do it ... Remember you earned your toy dinosaur; you can do it again!\"",
        "text_sha256": "8f1b41363555eb7524e4079049973dce40a7c6920109187473b78960fd30f095",
        "word_count": 57
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000054",
        "block_index": 54,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "How to phase out potty training rewards",
        "text_sha256": "386e8ac7c6aca53061d0867c21af30f0d5d1f5bfd68194653751a107e0af946c",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000055",
        "block_index": 55,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "As your child gets better at potty training (and yes, it will happen!), start to offer the reward every two or three times he uses the toilet, keeping track of his progress on a potty-training chart. Then, offer the reward for every five or six times he uses the toilet, and so on.",
        "text_sha256": "d680d8e4cb1a147f82871b14b3a050bcb210c957d244c575471cf163b8103c50",
        "word_count": 53
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000056",
        "block_index": 56,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Over time, even the most appealing of potty-training rewards will start to lose their attraction.",
        "text_sha256": "94457c2b9355f12ae05e1140cb843d95d37650661d5f912cda760d4d5d2ffdaf",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000057",
        "block_index": 57,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"As the child gains more independence and confidence, toileting becomes more like a routine,\" Zeltser says. \"Children look less towards their parents and rewards to reinforce the act of using the bathroom.\"",
        "text_sha256": "28a0cd2ef1f5dd9688c95c44390a864f8f7879b549e5e46c32e2722fc64f88ae",
        "word_count": 32
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 1038,
    "heading_count": 9
  },
